<pubDate>Mon, 19 May 2025 11:03:15 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Can we be normal about family policy?]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>There’s been a resurgence of interest this spring in “pro-natalist” policy, largely because of a conference on the subject in Austin that scored coverage in the New York Times and other media outlets. The conference itself seemed pretty heavily geared toward right-wingers, and the Trump administration, which has zero interest in bipartisanship or striking a reassuring posture on anything, keeps bringing it up, so the discourse has quickly become unhinged…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://www.slowboring.com/p/can-we-be-normal-about-family-policy?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://www.slowboring.com/p/can-we-be-normal-about-family-policy?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/economics-links-5192025">Economics Links, 5/19/2025</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.slowboring.com/p/can-we-be-normal-about-family-policy?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.slowboring.com/p/can-we-be-normal-about-family-policy?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 May 2025 11:03:15 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[The Last Gold Rush: AI and the New Mercantilism]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>By Jack Kieffaber and Garrett Maxwell…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://www.discoursemagazine.com/p/the-last-gold-rush-ai-and-the-new?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://www.discoursemagazine.com/p/the-last-gold-rush-ai-and-the-new?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/economics-links-5192025">Economics Links, 5/19/2025</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.discoursemagazine.com/p/the-last-gold-rush-ai-and-the-new?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.discoursemagazine.com/p/the-last-gold-rush-ai-and-the-new?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 May 2025 11:03:15 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Tariffs and Manufacturing Jobs: Three Big Problems]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>“American steelworkers, auto workers, farmers and skilled craftsmen… They watched in anguish as foreign leaders have stolen our jobs, foreign cheaters have ransacked our factories and foreign scavengers have torn apart our once beautiful American dream.” — President Donald Trump announcing his tariff strategy in a Rose Garden…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://agglomerations.substack.com/p/tariffs-and-manufacturing-jobs-three?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://agglomerations.substack.com/p/tariffs-and-manufacturing-jobs-three?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/economics-links-5192025">Economics Links, 5/19/2025</a></p>]]></description><link>https://agglomerations.substack.com/p/tariffs-and-manufacturing-jobs-three?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://agglomerations.substack.com/p/tariffs-and-manufacturing-jobs-three?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 May 2025 11:03:15 GMT</pubDate></item></channel></rss>